Id: cont005w
Severity: WARN
Category: containers
Check: check_containers
References: docker-run(1) --pid

A running container shares the host's process namespace (--pid=host,
pid: host in compose). Everything in it sees every process on the host,
their command lines and environment included, which often hold
passwords, and a root process in it can signal or trace the host's
processes. Monitoring agents use it; little else should.

To fix it, remove --pid=host, or confine the container that needs it
as far as it allows (read-only, no added capabilities).
